---
import LegalLayout from '../components/LegalLayout.astro';
const S = [
  { id: 'summary', title: 'In short' },
  { id: 'used', title: 'What this website stores' },
  { id: 'maps', title: 'Maps' },
  { id: 'choices', title: 'Your choices' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'If this changes' },
];
---
<LegalLayout title="Cookies | Quantum BioTesting" description="Quantum BioTesting does not set cookies or use analytics. Maps are provided by OpenStreetMap." heading="Cookies" sections={S}>
  <section id="summary">
    <h2>1. In short</h2>
    <p>This website does not set cookies, does not use analytics or advertising trackers, and does not store anything on your device. That is why you will not see a cookie banner when you arrive. The one thing loaded from elsewhere is the map images described below.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="used">
    <h2>2. What this website stores</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Stored?</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Cookies</td><td>None are used</td><td>No</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Local or session storage</td><td>None is used</td><td>No</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Analytics or advertising</td><td>None is used</td><td>No</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Fonts and images</td><td>Served from this website, not from a third party</td><td>No</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Map images</td><td>Loaded from OpenStreetMap on pages with a map, without cookies</td><td>No</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Our hosting provider keeps standard server logs, such as IP address and pages requested, to run and secure the website. See the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="maps">
    <h2>3. Maps</h2>
    <p>The maps on our home and clinic pages come from OpenStreetMap. Your browser fetches map images from OpenStreetMap’s servers, which receive your IP address and browser details. These map images are served without cookies, and nothing is stored on your device. See the <a href="https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy">OpenStreetMap Foundation privacy policy</a>. Each clinic page also has links to open the address in Google Maps or get directions; those open in a new tab and Google’s own policies apply once you are there.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="choices">
    <h2>4. Your choices</h2>
    <p>There is nothing to switch off, because nothing is switched on. You can still block or delete cookies in your browser settings at any time.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="changes">
    <h2>5. If this changes</h2>
    <p>If we ever add analytics or other tracking, we will update this page and the Privacy Policy, and ask for your consent first where the law requires it. The date at the top of this page shows when it last changed.</p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
